e distribuyen según criterios legales.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 112 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 16.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.2 to 9.4. December accounts for 15% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 11% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 15. Contract [1], for 14,069.23 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. Small amounts just under the limit may reflect standard market pricing or necessary purchases, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of December contracts to see if they align with other contracts. Review awardee A’s contracts to determine if they repeat the same service or product. Look for patterns in contract types to assess if multiple contracts serve the same purpose.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["24ZSBKfasWYzjChw4z%2FXvw%3D%3D","DXu4p0YBJeM7%2B9FIQYNjeQ%3D%3D","Pz0R%2BQfQK2%2FkY6rls5tG9A%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}